      "writtenOn": "2020-12-09T06:05:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But what if the capport API has a venue info URL, but the networkAgent has capport data with a null venue info URL (and just the friendly name or user portal URL) ?\n\nI think the merging needs to be something like:\n\n  /**\n   * @param naData captive portal data from NetworkAgent\n   * @param apiData captive portal data from capport API\n   */\n  @Nullable\n  private CaptivePortalData mergeCaptivePortalData(@Nullable naData, @Nullable apiData) {\n    if (naData \u003d\u003d null || apiData \u003d\u003d null) {\n        return naData \u003d\u003d null ? apiData : naData;\n    }\n    final CaptivePortalData.Builder builder \u003d new CaptivePortalData.Builder(naData);\n    if (apiData.isCaptive()) builder.setCaptive(true);\n    if (apiData.getByteLimit() \u003e\u003d 0) builder.setBytesRemaining(na.getByteLimit());\n    [...]\n    if (apiData.getVenueInfoUrl() !\u003d null) builder.setVenueInfoUrl(na.getVenueInfoUrl());\n    [...]\n  }\n\nNote that the NetworkAgent also needs to send isCaptive. One way to do this for Passpoint can be to have Wifi always say true at first, then send false when it receives CMD_REPORT_NETWORK_STATUS that says the network validated.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6117,
        "startChar": 45,
        "endLine": 6117,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "37d1fa36202bd04cf4c73d7c7a3f9b8252c81683",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
